The class of the two-term complex [A → B] (B in degree 0) is [B] − [A], so ch(V(Λ) ∩^L Z(x)) = ch(O_{V(Λ)}) − ch(O(−Z(x))|_{V(Λ)}) = −Σ_{i≥1} c_1(O(−Z(x))|_{V(Λ)})^i/i!. Hence:
- c_{1,V(Λ′)}(x)·[V(Λ′)] = −Int_{V(Λ′)}(x);
- Lemma 6.4.6 holds with an extra factor (−1)^d, and so does Lemma 6.4.7: c_{V(Λ)} = (−1)^d (c(d)/c′(d)) Σ Int_{V(Λ′)};
- in the proof of Theorem 6.4.9, l ∘ K_{V(Λ)}(x) = −c_{V(Λ′)}(x)/d′!.
Corollary 6.4.8, Theorem 6.4.9 and Corollary 6.4.10 are unchanged, since their statements are invariant under an overall sign.
